es":"Each assert gets a reachable cover; an unreached cover marks the assert vacuous and evidence-void. Environment assumptions are listed per property and are never assumed of DUT outputs. No assertion appears in assume form. BMC results state depth. Prove claims require induction success.","implementation_specific_characterization":[{"id":"C1_residual_bound","question":"Does a k exist such that no master-m-sourced forward occurs more than k cycles after a CYC drop with no new acceptance?","assumptions":["rev 2e8d3bc2 RTL","the exact parameters","K11"],"method":"cover search to find the max observed k, then attempt to prove for that k","use":"Only certified results may later enable discarding identities. A certificate requires a freeze and review. Never a guessed bound."},{"id":"C2_survivor_set","question":"Which buffered entries survive partial propagation?","method":"cover enumeration","use":"Descriptive only."},{"id":"C3_forward_order","question":"Is per-master forward order (per slave, across slaves) preserved?","method":"prove or cex","use":"Characterization only. Not a contract claim unless certified and separately registered."},{"id":"C4_timeout","question":"Does a mapped ERR without a slave ERR occur only when OPT_TIMEOUT or starvation conditions hold?","method":"prove under RTL","use":"May later reclassify unexplained_mapped_err with a certificate."}]},"synthetic_control_assessments":[{"name":"cross_slave/early_forward_ordered_retirement","assessment":"M0 reads 0x05 (slave0) then 0x15 (slave1). Slave1 is forwarded first. Slave ACK data: 0x98765432 on slave1, 0x1234ABCD on slave0. Master retires 0x1234ABCD then 0x98765432, which is correct per K6/K7. The prior checker wrongly reported a routing_payload violation.","label":"scoped_pass","basis":"K5 is unknown, so forward order is not judged. K6 is inferred. The pass covers order and data only and makes no forward-order claim."},{"name":"cross_slave/wrong_retirement_data","assessment":"Same trace, but the first master ACK delivers 0x98765432, which is the younger request's data.","label":"dut_violation","basis":"No hypothesis survives K6+K7. The label rests on inferred K6 (README) and must be stated as such."},{"name":"ambiguity/identical_requests_later_responses","assessment":"Both masters read 0x05. Two forwards occur. Slave data is 0x1234ABCD then 0x98765432. M0 gets the first, m1 the second.","label":"scoped_pass","basis":"The hypothesis with forward1 owned by m1 dies because m1 would need 0x1234ABCD. One surviving hypothesis remains. Ownership is reported as 'unique by elimination under the reference', not as proof of hidden state."},{"name":"ambiguity/followed_by_distinct_work","assessment":"The later distinct read 0x07 returns 0x88888877, which is correct.","label":"scoped_pass","basis":"The component closed and checking resumed. The whole epoch is not disabled."},{"name":"ambiguity/later_data_corruption","assessment":"The later read delivers 0x88888876 while the slave returned 0x88888877.","label":"dut_violation","basis":"The singleton component fails in all hypotheses."},{"name":"ambiguity/later_unaccepted_address","assessment":"The 0x07 request is forwarded as 0x0C. 0x0C routes legally to slave0, but no live or canceled identity matches it.","label":"dut_violation","basis":"K4 fails in all hypotheses. The later ACK is irrelevant to the label."},{"name":"ambiguity/inherently_indistinguishable","assessment":"Both slave ACKs carry 0x1234ABCD, so both hypotheses survive.","label":"scoped_pass","basis":"Observable clauses hold under every feasible history. Ownership is reported as indistinguishable(2). No hidden-owner claim is made. The label is not 'unresolved', because no unknown clause is relied on."},{"name":"prior selftests retained","tests":["write/read positive and faults","masked-lane","unmapped ERR/ACK","invented ACK","incomplete -> unresolved","unexplained ERR, persisting across reset","slave ERR","abort nonoldest/both/reverse -> unresolved","enabled-byte