ainst this matrix, including mutation checks. Each K-check is disabled in turn and must be caught by at least one control.","4. Write the formal harness: ghost FIFOs, symbolic tracked transaction, covers and false controls. Record the bmc/prove distinction. Characterization C1-C4 goes in a separate report, and any contract change requires a certificate and re-review.","5. Freeze the checker, controls and harness hashes, then perform immutable saved-action replay before live B/C.","6. Live B/C uses the original driver, budgets and traffic. No error suppression, forced reset, unique tags or one-outstanding restriction without a separately registered scope."],"unresolved":["Forward order (K5), the cancellation survivor set and latency (K9), and timeout/starvation eligibility (K8) are unknowable from public sources.","Hidden ownership of identical requests with identical responses is inherently indistinguishable.","Response order (K6) is inferred from README prose, not WB-normative.","No sound cancellation boundary other than reset exists without a certified C1. Canceled identities therefore persist, and residual forwards matching them stay unresolved.","DUT post-reset o_mack/o_merr and the eventual withdrawal of slave CYC after an abort remain unchecked.","Any pass is scoped to the checked clauses, the feasible-history semantics and the declared limits."],"ready_for_implementation":"true for checker v2, controls and formal harness implementation; false for live B/C until steps 2-5 are completed"}
